{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1855","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1855","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1855\",\"parent_revision\":\"e0b79d654abcf5ba4a532171cb45a5b1e882966b\",\"root_revision\":\"35556d5077ed159769f0b0583a0ad5b57ed893d678f1efd8f501e11006b84ef5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: Add token_budget field to Task/Plan models for per-task context bounds\\nDate: 2026-04-22\\nGoal: Add per-task token budget fields to Task and Plan models enabling context curation and cost prediction\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent is clear | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item body specifies exact fields, resolution rules (50/100/150%), and measurable signals\\n2. Scope boundaries are defined | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Code: models.py Task (line 114), Plan (line 258); server.py _sam_plan_ready (line 341); action_models.py; TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md; tests_sam/test_models.py\\n3. External interfaces (_sam_plan_ready compact branch) verified | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Tool:Bash: server.py:359-370 compact branch returns {id, task, agent, skills, dependencies, status, priority} \u2014 token_budget absent \u2014 verified 2026-04-22\\n4. Field alias convention confirmed | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Code: models.py:13 imports AliasChoices; lines 135-222 show consistent kebab-case/snake_case pattern for all fields\\n5. Implementation boundary defined (stop at MCP surface, not task-worker consumer) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item body: \\\"This item should NOT attempt to implement that consumer \u2014 it should stop at surfacing the field in the MCP response\\\"\\n6. Test file location is verified | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Tool:Bash: tests_sam/ directory confirmed present; test_models.py exists at plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py \u2014 initial item blocker was factually incorrect\\n7. Source pattern is cited | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Doc: research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 Context Curation and Token Budgeting, feature 2; 50/100/150% rule from decomposer.md\\nAVAILABLE count: 7\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 3 (external interfaces): PARTIAL \u2192 AVAILABLE (read server.py:359-370 \u2014 compact branch fields confirmed, token_budget absent)\\n- Condition 6 (test file location): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (tests_sam/ confirmed present with test_models.py \u2014 item blocker was wrong)\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add token_budget field to task/plan models for per-task context bounds** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: Context Curation and Token Budgeting (feature 2)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Context budget management is an observable quality gap (ad-hoc context curation leads to unpredictable token consumption) and is prerequisite for the Orchestra-derived context curation feature. The field addition itself is low-risk with established patterns. The downstream consumer (task-worker prompt injection) is explicitly out of scope for this item.\\n\\nEffort: Small \u2014 Two Pydantic field additions with established AliasChoices patterns, one server function update (add one key to compact dict), one doc file update, and unit tests for the resolution rule. Estimated 2-4 hours.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: any feature that reads `token_budget` to auto-curate context in the delegation prompt (Orchestra pattern, feature 2).\\n- Bottleneck: without this field, context assembly per task cannot be bounded or audited; cost prediction per task is impossible.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables per-task context budgeting aligned with the Orchestra pattern.\\n- Makes task complexity actionable beyond display purposes \u2014 `complexity` currently has no downstream consumer.\\n- Enables cost prediction: `default_token_budget * len(tasks)` gives an upper-bound token estimate for a plan.\\n- Prerequisite for a future `dh:task-worker` update to self-regulate context loading.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `sam_task(action='read')` is called for any task, the response includes a `token_budget` integer field representing the resolved effective budget for that task.\\n\\nWhen `sam_plan(action='ready')` is called, each ready-task entry includes a `token_budget` field.\\n\\nFor a plan with `default_token_budget: 80000`:\\n- A task with `complexity: low` and no override resolves to 40000 (50%)\\n- A task with `complexity: medium` and no override resolves to 80000 (100%)\\n- A task with `complexity: high` and no override resolves to 120000 (150%)\\n- A task with an explicit `token_budget: 60000` override uses 60000 regardless of complexity\\n\\nA task with no explicit budget and a plan without `default_token_budget` returns `None` (no constraint imposed).\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `Task.token_budget: int | None = None` added to `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` with kebab-case alias `token-budget` following the established pattern.\\n- `Plan.default_token_budget: int | None = None` added with alias `default-token-budget`.\\n- A resolution function (or property) that computes the effective budget: `Task.token_budget` overrides; otherwise complexity-based percentage of `Plan.default_token_budget`; `None` when plan has no default.\\n- `_sam_plan_ready` compact-branch dict includes `token_budget` key with the resolved integer value.\\n- `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` updated to document the new fields.\\n- A unit test file covering the resolution rules (test file to be placed in `tests/` \u2014 the `tests_sam/` directory referenced in the item does not exist).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n 'token_budget' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` returns at least two matches \u2014 one on `Task`, one on `Plan`.\\n2. `uv run sam schema --model Task 2>/dev/null | grep token-budget` exits 0 and prints the field definition.\\n3. `uv run sam schema --model Plan 2>/dev/null | grep default-token-budget` exits 0.\\n4. A plan YAML with `default-token-budget: 80000` and a task with `complexity: high` and no `token-budget` override: `sam_task(action='read')` for that task returns `token_budget: 120000`.\\n5. A plan YAML with `default-token-budget: 80000` and a task with `token-budget: 60000` (explicit override): `sam_task(action='read')` returns `token_budget: 60000`.\\n6. `sam_plan(action='ready')` compact output for a ready task includes a `token_budget` key.\\n7. `uv run pytest tests/ -k 'token_budget' -v` exits 0 and at least one test runs.\\n8. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` exits 0 (no linting regressions).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Primary source | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task (line 114) and Plan (line 258) Pydantic models |\\n| Action models | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 TaskDefinition (MCP boundary model inheriting Task) |\\n| Server implementation | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_sam_plan_ready` (line 336) is the target function for surfacing resolved budget |\\n| Existing tests | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam.py`, `tests/test_yaml_io.py` \u2014 SAM test patterns |\\n| Research source | `research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md` \u2014 Context Curation and Token Budgeting (feature 2); 50/100/150% rule from `decomposer.md` |\\n| Field alias pattern | All existing Task fields use `AliasChoices` with kebab-case and snake_case variants \u2014 see `blocked_by`, `parallelize_with`, `accuracy_risk` as canonical examples |\\n| Skill | /dh:development-harness (for model modification conventions) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 this is a pure model-field addition with no prerequisite items.\\n- Blocks: #1859 (autonomy modes) shares the Plan model and establishes a parallel pattern for adding plan-level fields; they are independent but inform each other's approach.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Adding two fields to Pydantic models with established alias patterns, updating one server function, updating one doc file, and writing unit tests for the resolution rule. No schema migration required (optional field with None default is backward-compatible). Estimated 2\u20134 hours of focused work.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:4fd064216d1b03ac402b470b44fd4599 -->\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- `tests_sam/` directory does not exist. The test path in the item's measurable signal (`tests_sam/test_models.py::test_task_token_budget_resolution`) is wrong. Must be resolved before writing the test.\\n- Delegation prompt injection point (how `task-worker` consumes `token_budget` from the ready-task response) is not specified. This item should NOT attempt to implement that consumer \u2014 it should stop at surfacing the field in the MCP response. A follow-up item is needed for the task-worker consumer side.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe development harness design intent (CLAUDE.md, development-harness CLAUDE.md) includes:\\n- Context-Fit Complexity Model: task complexity drives context sizing decisions\\n- No Invented Limits: callers control what they read; agents need explicit bounds to self-regulate\\n- Evidence discipline: context loading must be bounded and auditable\\n\\nAdding `token_budget` to Task and `default_token_budget` to Plan directly implements the \\\"context-fit\\\" design intent \u2014 complexity becomes actionable (not just a display label) and the token bound is explicit rather than ad-hoc. This is the prerequisite data model change for the Orchestra-pattern context curation feature referenced in the research entry.\\n\\nNo divergence detected.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail\\nRationale: The Task and Plan models lack a mechanism to bound context consumption per dispatched sub-agent. Without `token_budget`, agents operate without an explicit context contract \u2014 context curation is ad-hoc and cost prediction is impossible. This is a design gap where the system is missing a guardrail (context budget enforcement) that should be present to prevent unbounded context growth per task.\\nAnalysis method: Design intent review\\nScenario target: Any session where `/dh:implement-feature` dispatches tasks \u2014 all dispatched sub-agents operate without context bounds, which is the missing guardrail condition.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Add `token_budget: int | None` to Task, `default_token_budget: int = 80000` to Plan, complexity-based resolution, surfaced in `sam_plan(action='ready')` |\\n| Scope boundaries | PRESENT | `sam_schema/core/models.py`, `action_models.py`, `server.py`, `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, new SAM-model unit test |\\n| External interfaces | PARTIAL | `sam_plan(action='ready')` and `sam_task(action='read')` confirmed in code; task-worker delegation prompt injection point not verified |\\n| Constraints | PRESENT | kebab-case alias convention established; 50/100/150% rule from Orchestra research is sourced |\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | Task/Plan Pydantic models read; field alias pattern confirmed; `_sam_plan_ready` code path confirmed |\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | Three measurable signals given; unit test name specified |\\n\\n**Gaps requiring resolution before execution:**\\n\\n1. Test file path `tests_sam/test_models.py` does not exist \u2014 directory `tests_sam/` is absent. Actual SAM test files live in `tests/` (e.g. `tests/test_server_sam.py`, `tests/test_yaml_io.py`). The implementation task must create `tests/test_sam_models.py` (or equivalent) rather than `tests_sam/test_models.py`.\\n2. `_sam_plan_ready` compact branch (non-full) does not include `token_budget` in its returned dict (verified: returns only `id`, `task`, `agent`, `skills`, `dependencies`, `status`, `priority`). Adding `token_budget` to this branch is required to satisfy the measurable signal.\\n3. `dh:task-worker` delegation prompt injection point is unverified \u2014 the mechanism by which the resolved budget is written into the prompt is not described in the item and was not found in the codebase scan.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 This is a new feature addition. No existing behavior is broken or regressed.\\n\\nPre-condition verifiable: `grep -n 'token_budget' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` exits 1 (field absent before implementation).\\n\\nPost-condition verifiable: same grep exits 0 with at least 2 matches after implementation.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_task(action='read')` returns a `token_budget` key with an integer value.\\n- In a plan with `default-token-budget: 80000`, a task with `complexity: high` and no override resolves to `120000` when queried via `sam_plan(action='ready')`.\\n- New unit test `tests_sam/test_models.py::test_task_token_budget_resolution` verifies the resolution rules.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Downstream Consumers Read Only Not Modified By This Item\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `dh:task-worker` \u2014 currently ignores the field; a follow-up item will add delegation prompt injection\\n- `implement-feature` dispatch loop \u2014 passes task dict to task-worker; token_budget will be visible in ready output but unused until task-worker consumes it\\n- `sam_plan(action='ready')` callers \u2014 will see token_budget in compact output after this change\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`Task.token_budget: int | None` added to `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` with default `None` meaning \\\"use plan-level default\\\". `Plan.default_token_budget: int = 80000` added. When a task's token_budget is `None`, effective budget derives from `complexity` using a 50/100/150% rule against the plan default (matching Orchestra's decomposer pattern). The resolved budget is surfaced by `sam_plan(action='ready')` and written into the delegation prompt so `task-worker` can self-regulate its context loading.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Change Type | Impact |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` | Field addition | Task (line 114): add `token_budget: int \\\\| None = None` with AliasChoices; Plan (line 258): add `default_token_budget: int \\\\| None = None`. Resolution method added to Task. |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` | Inherited automatically | TaskDefinition inherits Task \u2014 new field available at the MCP boundary without explicit changes unless serialization overrides exist |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` | Compact-branch update | `_sam_plan_ready` (line 341): compact dict at lines 359-370 must add `token_budget` key with resolved value |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Documentation update | New fields `token-budget` and `default-token-budget` must be documented |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` | New tests | Resolution rule tests: low/medium/high complexity scaling, explicit override, None when no plan default |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nLow risk. All changes are additive:\\n- New fields have `None` defaults \u2014 backward-compatible with all existing plan YAML files\\n- No schema migration required\\n- No existing callers break \u2014 they receive an additional key in the compact dict\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact On Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe REFUTED claim about tests_sam/ being absent resolves Blocker 1 in the prior groomed content. The correct test file path is `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` \u2014 this directory already exists.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claims Verified\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Claim | Verdict | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"Task model has no token_budget field\\\" | VERIFIED | Tool:Bash: `grep -n 'token_budget' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2192 exit 1, no output (2026-04-22) |\\n| \\\"tests_sam/ directory is absent\\\" | REFUTED | Tool:Bash: `ls plugins/development-harness/tests_sam` succeeds; directory contains test_models.py among 20+ test files (2026-04-22) |\\n| \\\"_sam_plan_ready compact branch returns only id/task/agent/skills/dependencies/status/priority\\\" | VERIFIED | Code:Read: server.py:359-370 compact branch confirmed \u2014 seven keys only, no token_budget (2026-04-22) |\\n| \\\"AliasChoices used for kebab-case/snake_case aliases\\\" | VERIFIED | Code:Read: models.py:13 imports AliasChoices; lines 135-222 show consistent pattern on blocked_by, parallelize_with, accuracy_risk, etc. (2026-04-22) |\\n| \\\"Grep of plugin source shows zero occurrences of token_budget\\\" | VERIFIED | Tool:Bash: grep exit 1 confirms no matches in models.py (spot check); full grep not run but consistent with item creation context |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `Task` model at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` (lines 114\u2013223) has no `token_budget` field. It carries `complexity` and `accuracy_risk` but neither is consumed by any dispatcher or context-assembly code to bound the prompt size passed to `dh:task-worker`. Grep of the plugin source shows zero occurrences of `token_budget` or any per-task token cap.\\n\\nSymptom: sub-agents are dispatched without any explicit context budget, so context curation is ad-hoc. Token consumption per task cannot be predicted or audited before dispatch.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"03348371b60ac79956442460a4061c160b1fca922060a4957a87e0031f92901a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiI_Lg\"}"}